th the MacBook Air the CEO said they  would even beat the M2 Chip with the  help of former Apple Engineers but guess  what ended up happening we just got an  update last month saying that qualcomm's  Apple M1 slash M2 rival is finally on  the way but qualcomm's new Chips won't  be in devices until  2024 yes they delayed it again and those  nuvia chips aren't coming into consumer  PCS until 2024 I can't believe they  deleted once again now the crazy thing  is Apple's M3 chip yes their M3 is gonna  be launching late next year late 2023 in  devices already before the nuvia chip  that's supposed to come and beat the M1  and M2 which is only launching in 2024  which I see as an embarrassment because  this M3 Chip is going to be on tsmc's  three nanometer chip process and it is  going to be incredibly powerful much  more powerful than the M1 and the M2 and  then here's where we get into an even  bigger issue what does beating the Apple  M1 and M2 even mean does that mean  benchmarks does that mean real world  performance because Qualcomm recently  released their sq3 chip in the Surface  Pro 9 and let me remind you that this  was once seen as a M1 MacBook Pro killer  Yes people were speculating that the sq3  would destroy the Apple M1 chip but  check this out we just did a 2022 iPad  Pro versus Surface Pro 9 comparison  video and the results are downright  embarrassing the first thing I want to  point out is that the starting price for  the Surface Pro 9 with the sq3 chip is  1300 the same as the iPad Pro M2 with  the same RAM and storage configuration  and let me remind you that that's  actually more expensive than the M2  MacBook Air so yes this is an expensive  device but let me show you the  performance as you can see in single  core the M2 Chip absolutely destroys it  it's about 80 percent faster but then if  we go over to the multi-core the M2 is  50 faster so yes it is a lot faster but  it might not seem like that big of a  difference but wait until I show you the  